---
import DesignSystemShell from "../../layouts/DesignSystemShell.astro";
import DsSection from "../../components/design-system/DsSection.astro";
import DsRule from "../../components/design-system/DsRule.astro";
import DsSpec from "../../components/design-system/DsSpec.astro";

const files = [
  { file: "config/brand/assets/pro-exteriors-logo.svg", served: "/pro-exteriors-logo.svg", kind: "Primary horizontal lockup, full colour", status: "Official (client-supplied 350×180 'lgt')", use: "Light surfaces only: white, surface, surface-inset, light grey. The rail places it on a white chip.", note: "2.5 MB traced SVG wrapping a raster — fine for the app (cached), run through SVGO before any public site." },
  { file: "config/brand/assets/pro-exteriors-mark-square.svg", served: "—", kind: "Square lockup (500×500)", status: "Official", use: "App icons, social avatars, print where a square slot exists.", note: "Tight at favicon sizes; use the roof mark below 48px." },
  { file: "config/brand/assets/logo_color.png", served: "—", kind: "Full-colour raster, 620×210", status: "Derived from official", use: "Email signatures, documents, the fal.ai swag reference.", note: "sRGB; do not upscale beyond 100%." },
  { file: "config/brand/assets/pro-exteriors-logo-navy-transparent.png", served: "—", kind: "One-colour navy, transparent, 772×320", status: "Derived (WorkOS AuthKit light)", use: "One-colour reproduction on light surfaces; login screen.", note: "" },
  { file: "config/brand/assets/pro-exteriors-logo-white-transparent.png", served: "—", kind: "One-colour white, transparent, 772×320", status: "Derived (WorkOS AuthKit dark)", use: "One-colour reproduction on navy or dark surfaces; embroidery and screen print on dark garments.", note: "" },
  { file: "config/brand/assets/pro-exteriors-logo-white.svg", served: "—", kind: "Reversed vector, 620×210", status: "Cleverwork stand-in", use: "Dark surfaces where a vector is required.", note: "Placeholder geometry until the client supplies an official reversed export. Replace, do not extend." },
  { file: "app/command-center/public/favicon.svg", served: "/favicon.svg", kind: "Roof mark, 32×32", status: "Cleverwork stand-in", use: "Browser tab, PWA icon, the PE office badge on the map.", note: "Navy tile, gold roof, white base line. Swap for an official roof-only export when supplied." },
  { file: "app/command-center/public/brand-mark.svg", served: "/brand-mark.svg", kind: "Open Brain mark, 48×48", status: "Cleverwork", use: "OAuth resource_logo_uri for agent auth only.", note: "Navy tile, gold roof, white base, flag-red door. Never used as the company logo." },
  { file: "app/command-center/public/vendor-icons/pe-office-badge.png", served: "/vendor-icons/pe-office-badge.png", kind: "PE office map badge, 128×128", status: "Derived", use: "Territory Map office markers (46px).", note: "Roof mark on a white disc with a navy ring so our offices read differently from vendor branches." },
];
---

<DesignSystemShell slug="logo" source="config/brand/assets/README.md">
  <DsSection id="files" title="Approved files">
    <p>
      The canonical master is <code>config/brand/assets/</code>. Every other surface (the app's <code>public/</code>, the
      dashboard deployment, WorkOS) keeps a copy provisioned from there. Two artworks are official; the rest are derived or
      stand-ins awaiting official exports. <strong>Still needed from the client:</strong> an official reversed (white) logo
      and a tight roof-only mark.
    </p>
    <div class="ds-grid-2">
      <figure class="ds-figure">
        <img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt="Pro Exteriors LLC logo: a navy roof-line silhouette with the word PRO in navy on a white panel above the word EXTERIORS in flag-red italic capitals and a small LLC" width="620" height="210" style="padding:24px;background:#fff" />
        <figcaption>Primary lockup on white. Roof line and PRO in deep navy (#11133F); EXTERIORS and LLC in flag red (#C22326); two navy and two red rules frame the word.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="ds-figure">
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px">
          <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#11133f;border-radius:8px;padding:24px"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt="Roof mark on navy" width="64" height="64" /></div>
          <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:24px"><img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt="Primary lockup on a white chip as it appears in the rail" width="160" height="58" /></div>
          <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#f4f6f9;border-radius:8px;padding:24px"><img src="/vendor-icons/pe-office-badge.png" alt="PE office badge: roof mark on a white disc with a navy ring" width="46" height="46" /></div>
          <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#0a0c27;border-radius:8px;padding:24px"><img src="/brand-mark.svg" alt="Open Brain agent mark" width="48" height="48" /></div>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Roof mark (favicon), the rail chip, the PE office badge, and the Open Brain agent mark. Only the first three represent the company.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Served at</th><th>What it is</th><th>Status</th><th>Use</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {files.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{f.file}</code></td>
              <td class="nowrap">{f.served === "—" ? "—" : <code>{f.served}</code>}</td>
              <td>{f.kind}</td>
              <td class="nowrap">{f.status}</td>
              <td>{f.use}</td>
              <td>{f.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="anatomy" title="Anatomy">
    <p>The lockup is five pieces with fixed relationships. Proportions are read from the official 620×210 artwork; the unit <strong>x</strong> is the cap height of EXTERIORS (≈ 52px at 620 wide).</p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Piece</th><th>Ink</th><th>Relationship</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Roof line</strong></td><td>Navy</td><td>Spans ≈ 4.6x from the left eave to the chimney; the ridge sits ≈ 0.75x above the PRO panel's top edge. Never redrawn, never tilted.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>PRO panel</strong></td><td>Navy text on white, red underline</td><td>Panel is ≈ 2.4x wide × 0.95x tall, right-anchored under the roof's right slope. The red underline is ≈ 0.12x thick.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>EXTERIORS</strong></td><td>Flag red, 800 italic</td><td>Full width of the lockup (≈ 9.5x). Letterspacing +1 unit at 74px; tracking scales with size, it is never re-tracked by hand.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>LLC</strong></td><td>Navy, 800 italic</td><td>≈ 0.45x cap height, baseline-aligned to EXTERIORS, right-aligned to the S.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Rules</strong></td><td>Two red (top), one navy + one red (bottom)</td><td>Top rules flank the roof at eave height; bottom rules sit ≈ 0.3x below the wordmark baseline. They are part of the mark; never removed to "clean it up".</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="clear-space" title="Clear space & minimum size">
    <div class="ds-grid-2">
      <figure class="ds-figure">
        <div style="position:relative;background:#fff;padding:60px;border:1px dashed var(--error);border-radius:8px">
          <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;border:1px dashed var(--error);margin:0"></div>
          <img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt="Logo with the required clear-space zone drawn around it" width="400" height="135" style="display:block;border:0;background:#fff" />
          <span style="position:absolute;top:22px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);color:var(--error);font-size:11px;font-weight:700">roof height (r)</span>
          <span style="position:absolute;left:12px;top:50%;transform:rotate(-90deg) translateX(-50%);transform-origin:left;color:var(--error);font-size:11px;font-weight:700">r</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Clear space on every side equals the height of the roof mark (r). Nothing — text, another mark, a photo edge, a fold — enters the zone.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="ds-table-wrap">
        <table class="ds-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Context</th><th>Minimum</th><th>Below that</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Screen, horizontal lockup</td><td class="nowrap">120 px wide</td><td>Use the roof mark alone</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Screen, roof mark</td><td class="nowrap">16 px</td><td>—</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Print, horizontal lockup</td><td class="nowrap">32 mm (1.25 in) wide</td><td>Use the roof mark alone</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Print, roof mark</td><td class="nowrap">6 mm</td><td>—</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Embroidery</td><td class="nowrap">75 mm (3 in) wide; letter height ≥ 6 mm</td><td>One-colour version; drop the rules</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Pad print (pens)</td><td class="nowrap">25 mm wide</td><td>Wordmark EXTERIORS + PRO only, one colour</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Vinyl / signage</td><td class="nowrap">No minimum; maximum governed by the 2.5 MB SVG's raster — request vector from the client above 1 m</td><td>—</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="backgrounds" title="Backgrounds & variants">
    <p>Three approved colour treatments. Which one to use is decided by the surface, not by taste.</p>
    <div class="ds-grid-3">
      <figure class="ds-figure">
        <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:28px"><img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt="Full-colour logo on white" width="220" height="75" style="border:0" /></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Full colour on white / light.</strong> The default. Also correct on <code>surface-inset</code> (#f9fafb) and on light photography behind a solid white panel.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="ds-figure">
        <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#11133f;border-radius:8px;padding:28px"><div style="background:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 14px"><img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt="Full-colour logo on a white chip over navy, as in the rail" width="200" height="68" style="border:0" /></div></div>
        <figcaption><strong>White chip on navy.</strong> How the rail and any navy band carry the full-colour logo today. Chip radius 6px, chip padding 8px 14px, chip spans the rail width (Chris, TM-1, 2026-06-19).</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="ds-figure">
        <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;background:#11133f;border-radius:8px;padding:28px"><img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt="Placeholder for the one-colour white logo on navy" width="200" height="68" style="border:0;filter:brightness(0) invert(1)" /></div>
        <figcaption><strong>One-colour white on navy / dark.</strong> For garments, dark print and dark-mode marketing. Use the transparent white PNG or the white SVG stand-in; the preview above is a filter for illustration only — never ship a CSS-filtered logo.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-callout">
      <b>Dark mode in the app</b>
      <p>The app keeps the full-colour logo on its white chip in dark mode. The chip is part of the mark's presentation on any dark surface, so nothing changes when the theme flips (see <a href="/design-system/modes#media-dark">Modes</a>).</p>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="placement" title="Placement in the app">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Asset</th><th>Rendered size</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Side rail lockup</td><td><code>/pro-exteriors-logo.svg</code></td><td>Rail width (244px at 280 rail; 204px at 240), height auto, white chip radius 6px</td><td>Declared <code>width="160" height="58"</code> for aspect; CSS <code>width:100%</code>. Links to <code>/</code>. Alt: "Pro Exteriors".</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Auth denied page</td><td><code>/pro-exteriors-logo.svg</code></td><td>140×50</td><td>Standalone page without the shell; logo centred above the message.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WorkOS AuthKit</td><td>navy / white transparent PNGs</td><td>772×320 source; AuthKit scales</td><td>Light theme = navy, dark theme = white. Uploaded in the WorkOS dashboard, not served by the app.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Browser tab / PWA</td><td><code>/favicon.svg</code></td><td>16–32px</td><td>Roof mark only; the wordmark is illegible here.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Territory Map office marker</td><td><code>pe-office-badge.png</code></td><td>46px disc</td><td>Our offices must read differently from vendor branches at a glance.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Agent OAuth metadata</td><td><code>/brand-mark.svg</code></td><td>48px</td><td>Identifies the Open Brain resource server, not the company.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email (Maya, Casey)</td><td><code>logo_color.png</code></td><td>180px wide max</td><td>Inline, on white, with the r clear space. Never as the only content of an image-only email.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Generated PDFs (agreement package, invoice)</td><td><code>logo_color.png</code></td><td>38 mm wide at top-left</td><td>Header only; body carries no second logo.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="mark" title="Roof mark & favicon">
    <p>The roof mark is a Cleverwork stand-in that distils the official roof line into a tile: navy ground, gold roof, white base. It exists for the sizes where the wordmark cannot survive. It is not a second logo and never appears next to the lockup.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Roof mark at every size it ships" code="/favicon.svg">
      {[16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96].map((s) => (
        <div style="display:grid;gap:4px;justify-items:center"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt={`Roof mark at ${s} pixels`} width={s} height={s} /><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:11px">{s}px</small></div>
      ))}
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Tile radius is 6/32 of the tile size (18.75%) so it matches the app's 8px radius at 40px.</li>
      <li>The gold roof is the only place gold and navy meet without text; it is why the tab icon is recognisable in a row of navy tabs.</li>
      <li>Never recolour the tile to red or green to signal state — state is carried by the ring around a badge, never by the mark.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="vendor-badges" title="Vendor & office badges">
    <p>Map markers, legends and branch rows carry a vendor's own logo on an opaque white disc (transparent favicons washed out against the basemap). The <strong>ring</strong> carries status. Files: <code>public/vendor-icons/&lt;vendor&gt;-badge-&lt;state&gt;.png</code>, 128×128, rendered at 18px (legend), 36px (rows) and <code>round(scale × 4.2)</code> on the map.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Ring states, one vendor" code="abc-supply-badge-*.png">
      {["brand", "green", "yellow", "red", "grey"].map((s) => (
        <div style="display:grid;gap:4px;justify-items:center"><img src={`/vendor-icons/abc-supply-badge-${s}.png`} alt={`ABC Supply badge, ${s} ring`} width="48" height="48" /><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:11px">{s}</small></div>
      ))}
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Ring</th><th>Coverage lens meaning (docs/82, v2)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>brand</strong></td><td>Neutral — identity only, no status asserted (legend, rows, lists).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>green</strong></td><td>In-force, in-date price agreement for this branch and office.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>yellow</strong></td><td>Expired-evergreen agreement (still in effect) or the branch needs office routing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>red</strong></td><td>No agreement at all. QXO is red everywhere by design.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>grey</strong></td><td>Out of scope (outside drive time, inactive).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Only <code>abc-supply</code>, <code>srs</code> and <code>qxo</code> have badges; any other vendor falls back to a coloured circle symbol. Adding a vendor means adding the five ring files at 128×128 and the slug to <code>VENDOR_ICON_SLUGS</code>.</p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="misuse" title="Misuse">
    <p>Each of these has been seen or requested at least once. None ships.</p>
    <div class="ds-grid-3">
      {[
        ["Stretched", "transform:scaleX(1.35)", "Aspect ratio is fixed. Set one dimension and let the other follow."],
        ["Recoloured", "filter:hue-rotate(120deg)", "The inks are the brand. No green, no black-and-gold, no vendor colours."],
        ["Shadowed", "filter:drop-shadow(0 6px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.5))", "No drop shadows, glows, outlines or bevels."],
        ["Rotated", "transform:rotate(-8deg)", "Always level. The roof is the horizon."],
        ["Low contrast", "opacity:.35", "Never as a watermark or a ghosted background."],
        ["Full colour on navy without a chip", "", "Navy roof vanishes into navy. Use the white chip or the one-colour white version."],
      ].map(([title, style, why]) => (
        <figure class="ds-figure">
          <div style={`display:grid;place-items:center;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;background:${title.includes("navy") ? "#11133f" : "#fff"};border:1px solid var(--border)`}>
            <img src="/pro-exteriors-logo.svg" alt={`Misuse example: ${title}`} width="180" height="61" style={`border:0;${style}`} />
          </div>
          <figcaption><strong style="color:var(--error)">✕ {title}.</strong> {why}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="logo-motion" title="Logo motion">
    <p>
      The logo moves in exactly one way: a <strong>roof draw-in</strong> used for a first paint or a loading state on a
      public page — the navy roof line strokes on from the left eave to the right in 350ms, then the wordmark fades up over
      200ms. It never bounces, spins, pulses or parallaxes. In the Command Center the logo does not animate at all; the
      app is a tool, not a splash screen. See the live example in <a href="/design-system/motion#logo-graphic">Motion</a>.
    </p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="logo-alt" title="Alt text for the logo">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>alt</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Logo is a link to home (rail)</td><td><code>alt="Pro Exteriors"</code></td><td>The link's purpose is the company; "logo" adds nothing a screen reader needs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Logo is decoration beside a text heading that already says the name</td><td><code>alt=""</code></td><td>Redundant announcement is noise. Keep the <code>img</code> so print styles work.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Logo is the only identification on a page or document</td><td><code>alt="Pro Exteriors LLC"</code></td><td>The legal name is the content.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Logo shown in this design system as a specimen</td><td>Describe what is seen</td><td>The reader is studying the artwork, so the description is the content.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Vendor badge on the map</td><td><code>alt="ABC Supply, in-force agreement"</code> (vendor + ring meaning)</td><td>The ring is information; the alt carries it.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <div class="ds-rules">
    <DsRule id="L-01" title="Full-colour logo on light surfaces only; white chip or one-colour white on navy and dark." source="config/brand/assets/README.md">
      <p>The rail's white chip is the reference treatment on navy. Never place the full-colour artwork directly on navy, red, gold or a photograph.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-02" title="Clear space equals the roof height on all sides; minimum width 120px on screen, 32mm in print." source="config/brand/assets/README.md">
      <p>Below the minimum, use the roof mark alone.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-03" title="The logo's flag red is part of the mark and does not count against the one-CTA rule, but no extra flag red is added around it." source="config/brand/assets/README.md; DSN-012">
      <p>A red button next to the logo is still the one CTA in that viewport.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-04" title="Never stretch, recolour, rotate, shadow, outline, ghost or filter the logo." source="this chapter">
      <p>CSS filters on the artwork are for this documentation's illustrations only.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-05" title="Stand-in assets (favicon, white SVG) are replaced by official exports when supplied, never extended into new stand-ins." source="config/brand/assets/README.md">
      <p>Ask the client for the reversed and roof-only exports; do not draw a third variant.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-06" title="State around a mark is carried by the ring and its label, never by recolouring the mark." source="VendorTerritoryMap.astro:454-470; docs/82">
      <p>Vendor marks keep their identity colours; PE offices keep the roof mark.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-07" title="One logo per surface. The wordmark and the roof mark never appear together." source="this chapter">
      <p>The tab icon and the rail lockup are different slots on different surfaces, not a pair.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="L-08" title="The Command Center logo never animates; the roof draw-in is a public-page first-paint only." source="Design.md 'Motion is minimal and purposeful'">
      <p>Loading states in the app use text ("Loading invoice detail"), never a spinning logo.</p>
    </DsRule>
  </div>
</DesignSystemShell>
